  <prompt><![CDATA[
Post-v1.3.1 owner feedback follow-on. Owner wants two OOB-style form
fields BELOW the RegardingResolver PCF on the `sprk_todo` main form
(formid eca59df4-1364-f111-ab0c-7ced8ddc4cc6):

  - "Regarding Record Number" (`sprk_regardingrecordnumber`) — 1/3 row
    width, RENDERED AS A HYPERLINK that opens the target record.
  - "Regarding Record Name" (`sprk_regardingrecordname`) — 2/3 row width,
    plain text.

Both fields are read-only display (the RegardingResolver PCF is the
writer via PolymorphicResolverService.applyResolverFields — SRFR-020/032).

Deliverables:
  1. New companion webresource `sprk_regardingrecordnumber_hyperlink.js`
     v1.0.0 that on form OnLoad transforms the record-number field cell
     into an anchor pointing at the target record via
     Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo({ pageType: "entityrecord", entityName,
     entityId }). Defensive: silent-fail if selector/attributes missing.
     Mirrors sprk_todo_regarding_presave.js IIFE + namespace pattern
     (Spaarke.SmartTodo.RegardingRecordNumberHyperlink, ns.VERSION = "1.0.0").
  2. sprk_todo main form modification (via solution round-trip through
     the existing SetRegardingWebResources solution or a new form-scoped
     solution): add a section under the RegardingResolver PCF binding
     that contains sprk_regardingrecordnumber (col 1 of 3) + sprk_regarding
     recordname (col 2-3 of 3), both `readonlyoutsidewriteoptimized="true"`.
     Register the new webresource on the form OnLoad event.
  3. Deploy webresource + form to spaarkedev1. Verify via MCP that
     webresource exists (type=3) and via `pac solution list` that the
     form-carrying solution imports cleanly.

Constraints:
  - ADR-006 host-scripting Path A exception per SRFR-061 canonical pattern.
  - DO NOT remove existing form fields or events. This is additive.
  - Backward-compat: older sprk_todo records without populated
    sprk_regardingrecordnumber render blank (webresource silent-fails on
    missing values).
  - Companion webresource is DEFENSIVE — never throws, logs warn on any
    lookup miss, does not block form load.
  - DOM-manipulation fragility acknowledged: if selector [data-lp-id]
    fails, the webresource falls back to querySelector on common
    field-cell shapes. Test empirically after import.
  - No PCF change. No shared-lib change. STANDARD rigor (form config +
    webresource only).

Step 9.5 quality gates: SKIPPED per STANDARD rigor + user directive
(form config, not code).

Deploy targets: spaarkedev1. Use existing SetRegardingWebResources
solution (already at v1.0.0) for the webresource. For form: preferred
approach is targeted solution containing the sprk_todo main form only
(create SetRegardingFormPatch or add to SetRegardingWebResources by
adding the systemform component).
  ]]></prompt>

  <role>Dataverse form-scripting + FormXml developer familiar with
  MDA main-form section layout, systemform export/import roundtrip via
  PAC CLI + solution unpack, defensive JavaScript webresource patterns
  (see `src/client/webresources/js/sprk_todo_regarding_presave.js` and
  `sprk_fieldmapping_push.js`), and the Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo API
  for opening a target polymorphic record.</role>

  <goal><![CDATA[
Owner-visible outcome: on the sprk_todo main form, BELOW the
RegardingResolver PCF (bound to sprk_regardingrecordtype), a new
section renders two OOB-styled read-only fields:
  - "Regarding Record Number" (1/3 width) as a CLICKABLE HYPERLINK that
    opens the target record identified by sprk_regardingrecordtype +
    sprk_regardingrecordid (in a modal via Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo).
  - "Regarding Record Name" (2/3 width) as plain read-only text.

Both webresource + form deployed to spaarkedev1. On sprk_todo record
open, DevTools console shows the webresource init log
("[SmartTodo.RegardingRecordNumberHyperlink v1.0.0] ..."), and clicking
the record-number opens the correct target record. Backward-compat: v1.3.1
RegardingResolver PCF continues to function unchanged.
  ]]></goal>

