  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-006">Host-scripting webresource Path A pattern (per SRFR-061 canonical). Additive form event registration only; do not replace/remove existing OnLoad handlers.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Companion webresource is defensive: silent-fail (console.warn, no throw) on missing DOM selector, missing form attributes, or missing target-record type mapping.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Field additions preserve existing form behavior. RegardingResolver PCF binding on sprk_regardingrecordtype is UNCHANGED. `sprk_todo_regarding_presave.js` OnLoad handler is UNCHANGED.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Both new fields are `readonlyoutsidewriteoptimized="true"` — the PCF is the writer; the form displays what the PCF/presave persisted.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Webresource references `sprk_regardingrecordtype` (lookup to sprk_recordtype_ref) + `sprk_regardingrecordid` (text GUID) to compose the navigateTo target. Reads the linked entity name via the lookup entity metadata from the recordtype-ref lookup value (SDK-provided entityType, no extra query).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">STANDARD rigor: Step 9.5 quality gates SKIPPED per user directive (form config + host-scripting webresource, not TypeScript/C# implementation).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Model-Driven App form config + host-scripting webresource patterns + Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo</topic>
    <files>
      <file>src/client/webresources/js/sprk_todo_regarding_presave.js</file>
      <file>src/client/webresources/js/sprk_fieldmapping_push.js</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Defensive IIFE + namespace webresource" location="src/client/webresources/js/sprk_todo_regarding_presave.js">
        Namespace `Spaarke.SmartTodo.{Feature}` seeded from window; IIFE
        exposes `ns.VERSION` + `ns.onLoad(executionContext)`. Never throws:
        wraps body in try/catch + console.error prefix with version tag.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo for target-record open" location="src/client/webresources/js/sprk_fieldmapping_push.js">
        `Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo({ pageType: 'entityrecord', entityName,
        entityId }, { target: 2, width: { value: 80, unit: '%' }, height:
        { value: 80, unit: '%' } })`. `target: 2` = dialog modal;
        `target: 1` = inline (default). Catch and warn on failure.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <context>
    <background>
      Owner reviewed v1.3.1 RegardingResolver post-deploy (SRFR-034) and
      requested OOB-style form fields BELOW the PCF for the two most
      commonly needed values (record number + record name). Rationale:
      makers who prefer OOB form-field display over the PCF's Row-2
      inline hyperlink can now surface those values as normal form
      fields, with the record-number field additionally rendered as a
      clickable hyperlink to the target record (mirrors PCF Row-2 SRFR-034
      behavior for consistency).

      Form ID confirmed via MCP: `eca59df4-1364-f111-ab0c-7ced8ddc4cc6`
      ("To Do main form"). Solution ownership: SpaarkeMaster + Cr2b7d5.
      Existing webresource solution: `SetRegardingWebResources` v1.0.0
      (natural home for the new webresource).
    </background>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="SRFR-034" status="completed">RegardingResolver v1.3.1 deployed. The form config here does NOT depend on the PCF version but is authored assuming v1.3.1 is the live PCF.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
    <related-work>
      <item>No downstream tasks blocked. SRFR-084 UAT continues after this lands.</item>
      <item>Parallel: SRFR-035 (if concurrent) bumps PCF to v1.3.2 with auto-refresh. Different surface (PCF vs form XML + new webresource) — no collision.</item>
    </related-work>
  </context>

  <steps>
    <step order="0" name="Context Check">Confirm context &lt; 60%. Confirm SetRegardingWebResources solution exists at v1.0.0 and sprk_todo form ID via MCP.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Author companion webresource">Create `src/client/webresources/js/sprk_regardingrecordnumber_hyperlink.js` v1.0.0. IIFE + namespace `Spaarke.SmartTodo.RegardingRecordNumberHyperlink`. Public entry: `ns.onLoad(executionContext)`. Uses a bounded polling loop (max 20 attempts × 200ms = 4s) to wait for the field DOM to render, then transforms the field's display element into an anchor pointing at target via `Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo({pageType:'entityrecord', entityName, entityId}, {target:2, width:{value:80,unit:'%'}, height:{value:80,unit:'%'}})`. Reads entityName from `formContext.getAttribute('sprk_regardingrecordtype').getValue()[0].name`. Silent-fail on any miss.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Export existing webresource solution">Use PAC CLI to export the current SetRegardingWebResources solution as unmanaged to a temp directory (or use existing project scripts if available). This gives us the baseline to add the new webresource to.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Deploy webresource via MCP or Web API">Since form-only solution round-trip via SetRegardingWebResources adds risk to already-published fields, use direct webresource create/publish via MCP: create a new webresource record with name `sprk_regardingrecordnumber_hyperlink`, displayname, webresourcetype=3 (JScript), content base64-encoded. Add to SetRegardingWebResources solution component list. Publish. This is the minimal-blast-radius approach.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Export sprk_todo form for modification">Export the smallest possible solution containing the sprk_todo main form (formid eca59df4-1364-f111-ab0c-7ced8ddc4cc6). Approach: create a temporary form-scoped solution `SetRegardingTodoForm` via `pac solution init` in a temp dir; add the form component; export unmanaged; unpack; modify FormXml.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Modify FormXml">In the unpacked FormXml (`Entities/sprk_todo/FormXml.xml` or similar):
      (a) Locate the tab/section carrying the RegardingResolver PCF binding on `sprk_regardingrecordtype`.
      (b) Add a new section below it (or extend existing) with a 3-column-friendly layout carrying two cells: sprk_regardingrecordnumber (colspan=1) + sprk_regardingrecordname (colspan=2). Both cells `disableViewsForForm="1"` if needed; both fields `readonly` at the control level.
      (c) In `<formLibraries>`, add `<Library name="sprk_regardingrecordnumber_hyperlink" libraryUniqueId="{new guid}" />`.
      (d) In `<events>` element (create if absent), add an `<event name="onload">` handler pointing at `Spaarke.SmartTodo.RegardingRecordNumberHyperlink.onLoad` with `passExecutionContext="true"` and `enabled="true"`. Do NOT replace any existing OnLoad handlers.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Repack + import">Repack the modified solution and import via `pac solution import --path ... --publish-changes`. Verify import log for errors.</step>
    <step order="7" name="Verify">
      (a) Via MCP `read_query`: confirm `sprk_regardingrecordnumber_hyperlink` webresource exists with `webresourcetype = 3`.
      (b) Via MCP: confirm sprk_todo systemform has both fields present in FormXml (query systemform.formxml LIKE '%sprk_regardingrecordnumber%').
      (c) Owner-side smoke test: open a sprk_todo record in spaarkedev1, verify DevTools console log from webresource + hyperlink render + click-navigates to target. (This is deferred to owner UAT; the task itself completes when webresource + form are imported cleanly.)
    </step>
    <step order="8" name="Log + TASK-INDEX update">Write session log to `projects/set-regarding-and-field-mapping-resolver-r1/notes/task-036-sprk-todo-form-config.log`. Add SRFR-036 row to TASK-INDEX.md under Wave 3 post-v1.3.1 follow-on.</step>
    <step order="9" name="Update task status">Mark SRFR-036 completed. Reset current-task.md.</step>
  </steps>

